-- src:4783 | 3. אי־רישום או אי־תשלום לתקופה שעולה על 12 חודשים עד עשרים פעמים השכר הממוצע כמשמעותו בסעיף 2(ב), ולא יותר מסכום השווה לגמלאות בכסף ששילם המוסד לעובד או שהוא עתיד לשלמן

§§ `Which period: forks K1 to K3`

@ref NOTES.md fork K1
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 369(a) does not say to what day the period that elapsed runs, and the answer turns on it` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 369(a) does not say to what day the period that elapsed runs, and the answer turns on it"

@ref NOTES.md fork K2
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Schedule K1 prints cash benefits only, and section 369(a) charges benefits in kind too, and the answer turns on it` MEANS
    REFUSE "Schedule K1 prints cash benefits only, and section 369(a) charges benefits in kind too, and the answer turns on it"

@ref NOTES.md fork K3
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Schedule K1 has no row for a breach of 30 days or less, and the answer turns on it` MEANS
    REFUSE "Schedule K1 has no row for a breach of 30 days or less, and the answer turns on it"

@ref Schedule K1 (source lines 4775-4784)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the period that elapsed cannot end before it began` MEANS
    REFUSE "the period that elapsed cannot end before it began"

@ref NOTES.md forks K1 to K3
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
      `one`      IS AN a
      `other`    IS AN a
      `refusal`  IS AN a
GIVETH AN a
`Schedule K1 — the answer if` `one` `and` `other` `agree, or else` `refusal` MEANS
    IF `one` EQUALS `other` THEN `one` ELSE `refusal`

§§ `Column A: the row of the breach period`

-- The multiple of the average wage that column B allows for a breach from `start` to `end`: 5, 10 or 20 for the three rows, 0 where the
-- reading of a breach of 30 days or less says no charge may be made, NOTHING where it says the multiple limb does not bind.
-- "More than 30 days and not more than 6 months": more than 30 days elapsed, and the end is not after the day 6 months after the start.
@ref Schedule K1 column A, items 1 to 3 (source lines 4781-4783)
GIVEN start IS A DATE
      end   IS A DATE
      r     IS A `A reading of a breach of 30 days or less in Schedule K1`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Schedule K1 — the multiple of the average wage for a breach from` start `to` end `, reading a breach of 30 days or less as` r MEANS
    BRANCH IF Day end LESS THAN Day start                                      THEN `the period that elapsed cannot end before it began`
           IF Day end MINUS Day start AT MOST 30                               THEN `breach of 30 days or less` r
           IF Day end AT MOST Day (`add months` start 6)                       THEN JUST 5
           IF Day end AT MOST Day (`add months` start 12)                      THEN JUST 10
           OTHERWISE                                                                JUST 20
    WHERE
        `breach of 30 days or less` x MEANS
            CONSIDER x
            WHEN `no charge may be made for a breach of 30 days or less`              THEN JUST 0
            WHEN `a breach of 30 days or less is limited by the benefits limb alone`  THEN NOTHING
            WHEN `a breach of 30 days or less is declined`                            THEN `Schedule K1 has no row for a breach of 30 days or less, and the answer turns on it`

§§ `Column B: the most the clerk may charge`

-- Readings fully chosen (none declined).
@ref Schedule K1 column B (source lines 4781-4783); s 369(a) (source line 4015)
GIVEN b  IS AN `An employer's breach, for Schedule K1`
      aw IS A NUMBER
      rs IS A `The readings of Schedule K1`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Schedule K1 — the most the clerk may charge, readings chosen: breach` b `, average wage` aw `, readings` rs MEANS
    CONSIDER `the multiple`
    WHEN NOTHING   THEN `the benefits limb`
    WHEN JUST m    THEN min (m TIMES aw) (`the benefits limb`)
    WHERE
        `the end of the period` MEANS
            CONSIDER rs's `for the period that elapsed`
            WHEN `the period runs to the day of the insured event`                                  THEN b's `the day of the insured event`
            WHEN `the period runs to the day the arrears were paid or the employer registered`      THEN b's `the day the arrears were paid or the employer registered`
            WHEN `the period that elapsed is declined`                                              THEN `section 369(a) does not say to what day the period that elapsed runs, and the answer turns on it`
        `the multiple` MEANS
            `Schedule K1 — the multiple of the average wage for a breach from` (b's `the day the payment was due under section 353, or the day the employer should have registered under section 379`) `to` `the end of the period` `, reading a breach of 30 days or less as` (rs's `for a breach of 30 days or less`)
        `the benefits limb` MEANS
            CONSIDER rs's `for the benefits limb`
            WHEN `the limb counts cash benefits only, as Schedule K1 prints`                                                    THEN b's `the cash benefits the Institute paid or will pay`
            WHEN `the limb counts cash benefits and the money value of benefits in kind, as section 369(a) does`               THEN (b's `the cash benefits the Institute paid or will pay`) PLUS (b's `the money value of the benefits in kind given`)
            WHEN `the benefits limb is declined`                                                                                THEN `Schedule K1 prints cash benefits only, and section 369(a) charges benefits in kind too, and the answer turns on it`

-- The three switches, each declined reading put as each reading it stands for.
@ref NOTES.md forks K1 to K3 (SHRUG, Meng 2026-10-08)
GIVEN b  IS AN `An employer's breach, for Schedule K1`
      aw IS A NUMBER
      rs IS A `The readings of Schedule K1`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Schedule K1 — the most the clerk may charge: breach` b `, average wage` aw `, reading Schedule K1 as` rs MEANS
    CONSIDER rs's `for the period that elapsed`
    WHEN `the period that elapsed is declined` THEN
        `Schedule K1 — the answer if` (`again` (`with the period read as` `the period runs to the day of the insured event`))
            `and` (`again` (`with the period read as` `the period runs to the day the arrears were paid or the employer registered`))
            `agree, or else` `section 369(a) does not say to what day the period that elapsed runs, and the answer turns on it`
    OTHERWISE
        CONSIDER rs's `for the benefits limb`
        WHEN `the benefits limb is declined` THEN
            `Schedule K1 — the answer if` (`again` (`with the benefits limb read as` `the limb counts cash benefits only, as Schedule K1 prints`))
                `and` (`again` (`with the benefits limb read as` `the limb counts cash benefits and the money value of benefits in kind, as section 369(a) does`))
                `agree, or else` `Schedule K1 prints cash benefits only, and section 369(a) charges benefits in kind too, and the answer turns on it`
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER rs's `for a breach of 30 days or less`
            WHEN `a breach of 30 days or less is declined` THEN
                `Schedule K1 — the answer if` (`again` (`with a short breach read as` `no charge may be made for a breach of 30 days or less`))
                    `and` (`again` (`with a short breach read as` `a breach of 30 days or less is limited by the benefits limb alone`))
                    `agree, or else` `Schedule K1 has no row for a breach of 30 days or less, and the answer turns on it`
            OTHERWISE `Schedule K1 — the most the clerk may charge, readings chosen: breach` b `, average wage` aw `, readings` rs
    WHERE
        `again` x MEANS `Schedule K1 — the most the clerk may charge: breach` b `, average wage` aw `, reading Schedule K1 as` x
        `with the period read as` y MEANS `The readings of Schedule K1` WITH `for the period that elapsed` IS y, `for the benefits limb` IS rs's `for the benefits limb`, `for a breach of 30 days or less` IS rs's `for a breach of 30 days or less`
        `with the benefits limb read as` y MEANS `The readings of Schedule K1` WITH `for the period that elapsed` IS rs's `for the period that elapsed`, `for the benefits limb` IS y, `for a breach of 30 days or less` IS rs's `for a breach of 30 days or less`
        `with a short breach read as` y MEANS `The readings of Schedule K1` WITH `for the period that elapsed` IS rs's `for the period that elapsed`, `for the benefits limb` IS rs's `for the benefits limb`, `for a breach of 30 days or less` IS y

@ref NOTES.md forks K1 to K3 (SHRUG, Meng 2026-10-08)
GIVETH A `The readings of Schedule K1`
`Schedule K1 — the readings this row takes where the texts do not decide` MEANS
    `The readings of Schedule K1` WITH
        `for the period that elapsed`   IS `the period that elapsed is declined`
        `for the benefits limb`         IS `the benefits limb is declined`
        `for a breach of 30 days or less` IS `a breach of 30 days or less is declined`

-- The charge itself is the cash benefits and the money value of benefits in kind (s 369(a)), up to the most the clerk may charge.
@ref s 369(a) (source line 4015); Schedule K1 column B (source lines 4781-4783)
GIVEN b  IS AN `An employer's breach, for Schedule K1`
      aw IS A NUMBER
      rs IS A `The readings of Schedule K1`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 369(a) — the most the Institute can charge the employer: breach` b `, average wage` aw `, reading Schedule K1 as` rs MEANS
    min ((b's `the cash benefits the Institute paid or will pay`) PLUS (b's `the money value of the benefits in kind given`))
        (`Schedule K1 — the most the clerk may charge: breach` b `, average wage` aw `, reading Schedule K1 as` rs)

@ref s 369(a) (source line 4015)
GIVEN b  IS AN `An employer's breach, for Schedule K1`
      aw IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 369(a) — the most the Institute can charge the employer: breach` b `, average wage` aw MEANS
    `s 369(a) — the most the Institute can charge the employer: breach` b `, average wage` aw `, reading Schedule K1 as` (`Schedule K1 — the readings this row takes where the texts do not decide`)
